@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF4FB
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #355777
skinparam ActorBorderColor #355777
skinparam ArrowColor #355777
hide footbox
autonumber
title Operator-only consistent user-data export

' Sources relative to repository root:
' backend/app/export_user.py

actor Operator
participant "app.export_user" as Export
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant "Private output file" as File
Operator -> Export : python -m app.export_user --user-id UUID --output NEW_PATH
Export -> DB : Connect; REPEATABLE READ; BEGIN; SET TRANSACTION READ ONLY
note right of DB : PostgreSQL uses one consistent read-only snapshot.\nOther dialects use their normal transaction behavior.
Export -> DB : Select account by ID using explicit export fields
break User missing
  DB --> Export : No account
  Export --> Operator : Exit 1; no export file created
end
Export -> DB : Read words, review states, attempts, session metadata\nand Common questions (including learning progress)
DB --> Export : User-scoped records from same snapshot
Export -> Export : Serialize versioned JSON; UUIDs and UTC timestamps\nExclude password hashes, tokens and token hashes, rate buckets
Export -> DB : End read transaction; close connection
Export -> File : Exclusive create with O_EXCL, permissions 0600
alt Existing destination / symlink
  File --> Export : FileExistsError
  Export --> Operator : Exit 1; existing path unchanged
else New file
  Export -> File : Write JSON; flush and fsync; close
  alt Write fails
    Export -> File : Remove incomplete new file
    Export --> Operator : Propagate failure
  else Write succeeds
    Export --> Operator : Success message; user data is not printed to stdout
  end
end
Export -> DB : Dispose engine in finally
note over Export : This is a CLI; there is no HTTP user-export endpoint.
@enduml
